# Standard Information Types
# This file classifies the information within a source by the informant's
# relationship to the event, following the Evidence Explained (Elizabeth Shown
# Mills, 4th ed., 2024) "information" axis: primary, secondary, or indeterminate.
# This axis is independent of source nature (see source-natures.glx): a single
# source can carry both primary and secondary information (e.g., a death
# certificate records the death firsthand but the deceased's birth date
# secondhand). When set on a source this property records the predominant or
# default information quality; fact-level variation is better expressed per item.
# Archives can extend this with custom values by adding additional entries.

information_types:
  primary:
    label: "Primary Information"
    description: "Reported by someone with firsthand knowledge — an eyewitness or participant recording at or near the time of the event."

  secondary:
    label: "Secondary Information"
    description: "Reported by someone without firsthand knowledge — secondhand, hearsay, or recorded substantially after the event."

  indeterminate:
    label: "Indeterminate Information"
    description: "The informant, or the origin of the information, cannot be determined, so its primary/secondary character is unknown. (Evidence Explained calls this 'undetermined'.)"
